# Empty QR Code — a tilted rounded tile that cycles a big Skia letter
# ("YOUR LOGO", one letter every 650 ms over a changing radial gradient);
# tapping it springs it upright and larger (scale 1.4, rotate -10deg -> 0deg)
# and fades the logo out to reveal a real QR code; tapping again reverses.
# What this test covers: letting the letter/gradient cycle run (setInterval +
# Skia text measured in a worklet), reveal and hide with springs settled,
# reversing mid-spring, a rapid tap burst, a press-and-hold, taps outside the
# tile (must not toggle), and the cycle continuing while the QR is shown.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/empty-qr-code"
wait 2000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 30000
wait 3000
# Reveal the QR, then hide it.
press 201 437
wait 1500
press 201 437
wait 1500
# Reverse mid-spring.
press 201 437
wait 150
press 201 437
wait 1500
# Rapid burst (odd: ends revealed).
press 201 437 --count 7 --interval-ms 90
wait 2000
# Taps outside the tile: no toggle.
press 60 700
wait 300
press 340 250
wait 300
# Hold then release: hides.
longpress 201 437 800
wait 1500
# Letters keep cycling.
wait 3000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
